# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
"""Assemble the MemVeil owner bundle from exact pinned inputs.

Builds the distributable binary (``$ORIGIN``-relative RUNPATH),
ships the Mojo runtime closure plus the pinned native bridge and
BPF object, and records every payload hash in MANIFEST.json. A
source inventory sealed at build start verifies every
source-derived and build-output copy before staging ships; the
git revision stays descriptive next to the inventory digest.
Every archived file binds to its verified bytes as consumed,
and the tarball hashes before publication and again after the
rename, so bytes changed after verification fail the package.
Every shipped runtime file except the natively built bridge
traces to pinned package bytes: the packager fetches the locked
archives, verifies them against pixi.lock, and compares staged
bytes against archive members with explicit relocation
handling, recording owner, member, digests, and license texts
in the manifest.

Layout of ``dist/memveil-<version>/``::

    bin/memveil            relocatable binary (RUNPATH $ORIGIN/../lib)
    lib/*.so*              Mojo runtime closure + libbpf_mojo.so.1
    bpf/*.bpf.o            production BPF objects (attempt,
                           lifecycle, copy)
    profiles/              manifest plus shipped semantic profiles
    docs/                  the full manuals tree (every manual
                           quickstart/support reference ships)
    examples/real-capture/ sanitized real capture (worked example)
    examples/lifecycle-copy/ recorded three-channel capture
                           (worked example with oracle logs)
    LICENSE, LICENSES/   MemVeil's own license texts
    licenses/              third-party texts + libbpf-mojo's own
    THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES*   attribution (own + libbpf-mojo verbatim)
    MANIFEST.json          file hashes, versions, source revisions

Usage: tools/package [--out DIR] [--tag NAME]
  --out DIR   stage directory (default: dist/)
  --tag NAME  bundle directory name (default: memveil-<version>)

Requires LMB_PACKAGE (pinned libbpf-mojo tarball), a working
tools/build, and patchelf (apt install patchelf) to normalize the
bundle RUNPATH. Fails closed when the link closure names anything
outside the shipped lib/ set and the system allowlist.
"""

